WEBVTT

00:00:59.385 --> 00:01:01.955
it’s important to understand the 
difference between

00:01:01.955 --> 00:01:04.085
glaciers that grow in the wild,

00:01:04.085 --> 00:01:06.475
and those that humans create.

00:01:06.475 --> 00:01:07.375
In the wild,

00:01:07.375 --> 00:01:10.105
glaciers require three conditions to grow:

00:01:10.105 --> 00:01:13.855
Snowfall, cold temperatures, and time.

00:01:13.855 --> 00:01:17.375
First, a great deal of snow falls and 
accumulates.

00:01:17.375 --> 00:01:20.235
Cold temperatures then ensure that the 
stacked up snow

00:01:20.235 --> 00:01:24.325
persists throughout the winter, spring, 
summer, and fall.

00:01:24.325 --> 00:01:27.522
Over the following years, decades, 
and centuries,

00:01:27.522 --> 00:01:29.732
the pressure of the accumulated snow

00:01:29.732 --> 00:01:34.642
transforms layers into highly compacted 
glacial ice.